In article <1993Apr4.145639.22468@yang.earlham.edu>, marcs@yang.earlham.edu (Interface) writes:
|> 
|> 	I was just thinking of about it and thinking of some of the worst 
|> things that could happen to you in nethack without killing you outright, 
|> and getting a cursed ring of boots of levetation came to mind. If you don't 
|> have a scroll of remove curse, then you won't be able to pickup any new items. 
|> You mare survive if the following is true:
|> a) You have enough food to survive long enough for your god to be ready to 
|> help you.
|> b) There is a sink on or above your level, and you have enough food to get 
|> at it.
|> c) A nymph on or above your level may or may not help for the ring, and a 
|> Succubus will get the boots off. The nymph is problematic, because she is 
|> likely to rob other stuff and leave you in a bad spot.
|> 
|> The point of this post, was that there are some very simple things that 
|> can cause great problems. With other cursed items, you can at least pick 
|> up items that will help. Can anyone else think of any cursed items that 
|> would create more complications than just the obvious ones?

Welcome to NetHack -more-
Bad things can happen on Friday the 13th -more-
g - gray stone -more-
You are pinned, unabled to move.
[Messages paraphrased from memory]

Cursed lodestones can absolutely ruin your day.  Why? you can't even move,
much less pick stuff up.  You're even worse off then before?

a) have enough food so you can get help from your God.
b) hope a nymph drops by.
c) hope something else doesn't
d) If you're strong enough...drop lots of other things and find somewhere to
get remove curse.  (Usually doesn't happen with weaker creatures)

ObHack:  Had a tourist that started with a lodestone in a bag.  Because the
game allows you to carry what you started with, this 'Tourist' had an 18/**
strength at the beginning of the game.  The bag wasn't cursed, so I ditched
it!  BTW:  I was still stressed even with 18/** str and the lodestone.

